S. Student Staff Graduate Orientation Steps to Enroll Show more section nav three links Freshman Students Transfer Students Graduate Students International Students Show more section nav three links Freshman Students Transfer Students Graduate Students Intercampus Transfer Students Adult Students Summer Students Cost & Aid Show more section nav three links Cost of Attendance Show more section nav three links Undergraduate Costs Graduate Costs Net Price Calculator International Cost of Attendance Show more section nav three links International Undergraduate Costs International Graduate Costs Financial Aid Show more section nav three links Aid for International Students Scholarships Show more section nav three links International Student Scholarships Show more section nav three links C.V. Starr Foundation Scholarship Japan Alumni Chapter Scholarship Scott Schurz Latin American Scholarship BP Peduli Scholarship Bunchana Atthakor Scholarship Eoyang-Lee Fellowship Irving and Lena Lo (ILLO) Scholarship Fund Rising Star Scholarship Global Citizen Scholarship External Scholarships Grants & Fellowships Loans Pay Your Bill Campus Life Show more section nav three links Campus Traditions Community & Involvement Show more section nav three links Student Organizations Student Ambassadors Athletics & Recreation Housing & Dining Life in Bloomington Campus Events Show more section nav three links America 250 Show more section nav three links Revolution and Reflection Self-Guided Tour Small Grant Recipients Arts and Culture Campus Safety Campus Map, Parking & Transportation Show more section nav three links Getting to Campus Campus Buildings Driving & Parking on Campus Research Show more section nav three links Events & Workshops Innovation & Entrepreneurship Show more section nav three links Innovator Stories Centers, Museums, & Institutes Libraries In the News Student Research Opportunities Student Support Show more section nav three links Academic Advising & Support Career Services & Jobs Show more section nav three links Internships Part-time Jobs Mentorship & Coaching Health & Wellness Show more section nav three links Mental Health Resources Money & Essential Needs Campus Technology Show more section nav three links IU Account Setup Recruit IU Students Alumni & Giving Show more section nav three links Give to IU About Show more section nav three links History Rankings and Statistics Strategic Plan Bloomington Leadership & Administration Show more section nav three links About the Bloomington Chancellor Bloomington Chancellor's Cabinet Bloomington Vice Chancellors Campus Initiatives Show more section nav three links Campus Policy Committee Faculty & Staff Community Show more section nav three links Faculty & Staff Resources For the Glory Newsletter Show more section nav three links IU Foundation IU Foundation Ed Dallis-Comentale Michael Snow Alvin Rosenfeld Roberto Rodriguez Rita Patel Christoph Irmscher and David Polly Brea Perry, Bernice Pescosolido, and Kosali Simon Indiana Daily Student and Arbutus AAAS Fellows IU Debate Team Dana Habeeb Distinguished Professors Sarah Commodore Brian Yanites Brad Fulton Michael Wasserman Jingjing Zhang Pete Kollbaum Indiana University Football Paige Andersson and Rachael Jones McAfee Michel Chaouli Julia Kelson Jeremy Siek Philip Shushkov Monica Nesbitt Kevin Zumbrun Amar Flood Bernice Pescosolido Ore Koren Jacobs School of Music Paul Wright Bridger Ehli David Crandall Roger Innes Faculty Council Reports Show more section nav three links January 27, 2026 Faculty Council report January 13, 2026 Faculty Council report November 18, 2025 Faculty Council report November 4, 2025 Faculty Council report October 14, 2025 Faculty Council report September 23, 2025 Faculty Council report News & Communication Show more section nav three links State of the Campus Show more section nav three links 2026 State of the Campus Search the site Search Close search Part-time jobs Earn while you learn Working during college is about more than a paycheck. Whether you are looking for an on-campus role, a work-study position, or an off-campus job, employment at IU Bloomington helps you build a professional network, manage your time, and develop the skills employers value most. International student requirements Protecting your immigration status Federal regulations strictly limit the types of work international students can perform based on your specific visa status. Before you accept any job, contact the Office of International Services (OIS) to secure the necessary work authorization. Back to Academic Advising & Support menu Academic Advising & Support Back to Career Services & Jobs menu Career Services & Jobs Internships Part-time Jobs Mentorship & Coaching Back to Internships menu Internships Back to Part-time Jobs menu Part-time Jobs Back to Health & Wellness menu Health & Wellness Mental Health Resources Back to Money & Essential Needs menu Money & Essential Needs Back to Campus Technology menu Campus Technology IU Account Setup Student Support Academic Advising & Support Career Services & Jobs Career Services & Jobs menu Health & Wellness Health & Wellness menu Money & Essential Needs Campus Technology Campus Technology  menu Recruit IU Students Home Student Support Career Services & Jobs Part-time Jobs Why work during college? Maintaining a part-time job—even a summer role—demonstrates a strong work ethic and the ability to multitask. On average, IU students work 10–12 hours per week, allowing them to balance academics with professional growth. Build your resume: Develop the top skills employers seek, including problem-solving, teamwork, and communication. Fund your education: Earn money to help cover tuition, books, and living expenses. Expand your network: Increase your interaction with faculty, staff, and the Bloomington community. Discover your path: Test-drive different work environments to see what fits your interests and career goals. How do part-time jobs differ from internships? While both provide work experience, a part-time job is often focused on providing a service to an employer in exchange for wages. An internship is a more structured professional learning experience that specifically offers practical work related to your field of study and often includes academic credit or professional mentorship. Find the part-time job for you There are several ways to secure employment that fits your schedule and financial needs. On-campus student jobs Work for the university in various departments, libraries, or offices. On-campus roles often offer more flexibility around your class schedule. Federal work-study If you have a work-study award as part of your financial aid, you can pursue specialized positions reserved for eligible students. Off-campus employment The Bloomington community offers diverse roles in local businesses and organizations. When searching off-campus, prioritize employers who understand the demands of a student schedule. $10.15 IU (on-campus) minimum hourly wage $7.25 Indiana (off-campus) minimum hourly wage We are here to help Regardless of your major, year, or background, our team is available to help you find a role that fits your goals and help you manage your work-study award. For questions regarding on-campus, off-campus, and hourly employment, visit Career Exploration & Student Employment in the Wells Library. Contact your career coach IU Bloomington Career Exploration & Student Employment Herman B Wells Library\n1320 E. 10th Street\nBloomington, IN 47405 iucareer@iu.edu (812) 855-5234 Legal Accessibility College Scorecard Open to All Privacy Notice Required Disclosures Copyright © The Trustees of Indiana University"
    },
